<onlyinclude>The '''global brain''' is a research hypothesis and metaphor in which globally connected humans, organizations and digital systems collectively process information in ways compared with a brain.

== Explanation ==
Search engines, communications networks and collaborative knowledge platforms connect people and resources across the planet. The metaphor suggests studying how those connections help solve problems. It does not establish that the internet is a conscious organism or that a single mind controls it.

